  "name": null,
  "problem": "The following table shows the speed $v$, in $\\text{km/min},$ at certain times during a family car trip over a period of $60$ minutes.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{min})$ | $60$ | $70$ | $80$ | $95$ | $110$ | $120$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v\\,(\\text{km/min})$ | $1.5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1.5$ |\n\nAssuming that the family traveled $130\\,\\text{km}$ during the first hour of the trip, use the left Riemann sum to approximate the total distance traveled during the first two hours.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*",
  "worked_solution": "",
